{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/1284208815256360/posts/3028373867506504/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/groups/1284208815256360/posts/3028373867506504/","title":"Town of Davie | Attempting something way out of my comfort zone, but I think it could be beneficial in the long run | Facebook","description":"Attempting something way out of my comfort zone, but I think it could be beneficial in the long run. I attended a Board Of Governors meeting last night for the Pine Island Ridge Community. Every...","language":"en","text":"Attempting something way out of my comfort zone, but I think it could be beneficial in the long run. I attended a Board Of Governors meeting last night for the Pine Island Ridge Community. Every morning I see roughly 20-30 high school kids wait around this area for the bus. Plus, roughly 10 vehicles parking on the swale and such. It’s early, it’s dark, and of course…it’s hot. At the meeting last night I asked to speak in their open forum and suggested a covered structure of some kind be proposed so the kids wouldn’t have to wait by the road. With power and lighting as well. The area is a basically a green space right now with a few benches with no cover and really isn’t being utilized like it could be in my humble opinion. This used to be a playground. Now, I understand folks don’t like to see anymore concrete structures being erected in this town, but if it’s beneficial to many folks who live in the community and the funds are available without raising HOA fees. Why not think about it? It’s not just high school kids. It’s also middle schoolers, elementary kids, preschoolers, it could be a designated Uber and Lyft pick up/drip off. Then, it could possibly be rented for small events. Maybe add some bbq pits as well? If you live in Pine Island Ridge, I’d love to know if this is a good idea or a complete waste of time and resources. Thoughts, suggestions, ideas?\n\nAll reactions:\n\n31\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nShare\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nMaria Bruno\n\nI agree, at least a gazebo in the park area for them to wait!\n\n5\n\nView all 7 replies\n\nEmily Palacios Borens\n\nContact the Indians!\n\nLet them make one out of thatch. No concrete required.\n\nI also think it’s less expensive or there is no permit process. There’s something about that. …\n\nSee more\n\nElaine-Rose Fischer\n\nThe issue is that it’s a natural preserve. Which is why the playground got moved to near the tennis courts.\n\n5\n\nView all 2 replies\n\nView more comments\n\n3 of 10","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2160.449339004117,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}